.TH "BLOB.TEXTSTREAM" "3JS" "September 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Blob.textStream \- Blob: textStream() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]textStream()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]Blob\f[R]
interface returns a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] that can be used to read
the contents of the \f[CR]Blob\f[R] in chunks of UTF\-8.
.PP
This provides an easier mechanism for streaming the content than piping
a \f[CR]Blob.stream()\f[R] byte stream through a
\f[CR]TextDecoderStream\f[R].
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] The \f[CR]textStream()\f[R] method differs from
\f[CR]FileReader.readAsText()\f[R] in that it always uses UTF\-8
encoding, whereas \f[CR]readAsText()\f[R] has a parameter that sets the
encoding.
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
textStream()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reading blob content as a text stream
This example shows how to read blob content as a text stream.
.PP
We create a sample \f[CR]Blob\f[R], obtain a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R]
of its content using \f[CR]textStream()\f[R], then read the text via a
reader created using \f[CR]ReadableStream.getReader()\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] pElem = document.querySelector(\(dqp\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] obj = { hello: \(dqworld\(dq };
\f[B]const\f[R] myBlob = \f[B]new\f[R] Blob([JSON.stringify(obj, \f[B]null\f[R], 2)], {
  type: \(dqapplication/json\(dq,
});

\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] streamBlobText(blob) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] textStream = blob.textStream();
  \f[I]// instead of\f[R]
  \f[I]// const textStream = blob.stream().pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream());\f[R]

  \f[B]const\f[R] reader = textStream.getReader();

  \f[B]while\f[R] (\f[B]true\f[R]) {
    \f[B]const\f[R] { value, done } = \f[B]await\f[R] reader.read();
    \f[B]if\f[R] (done) \f[B]break\f[R];
    pElem.textContent += value;
  }
}

streamBlobText(myBlob);
.EE
